# Copy to `.env.remote` (gitignored). Use whatever **RDS** user/password your admin gave you —
# they do not need to match the local Docker user in `.env`. This whole `DATABASE_URL` replaces
# the one from `.env` whenever the overlay is loaded.
#
# Loaded after `.env` when:
#   MLBAPP_DOTENV=.env.remote pnpm dev
# or: pnpm dev:remote
# or: MLBAPP_DOTENV=.env.remote in your shell / in `.env`
#
# Flyway against this DB (Docker only; uses DATABASE_URL from this file):
#   pnpm db:migrate:remote
#   pnpm db:repair:remote
#
# JDBC → URI: strip the `jdbc:` prefix and use `postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@host:5432/dbname`
# If the password contains `@`, `:`, or `#`, URL-encode it (e.g. `p@ss` → `p%40ss`).
# Postgres URI — RDS user, RDS password, host, database:
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://RDS_USER:RDS_PASSWORD@YOUR_RDS_HOST:5432/postgres
#
# Optional: RDS-only tuning (examples)
# PGSSLMODE=require
